                    KAIRA OASIS CARE LLC
              COLLEGE OF DIRECT SUPPORT PROGRAM
              Training & Professional Development
================================================================================

PROGRAM OVERVIEW
================================================================================

The College of Direct Support (CDS) is a comprehensive professional development 
program designed to enhance the knowledge, skills, and competencies of direct 
support professionals working in healthcare and hospice care settings.

PROGRAM OBJECTIVES
================================================================================

Upon completion of this training program, participants will be able to:

✓ Understand the principles of person-centered care
✓ Develop effective communication and interpersonal skills
✓ Recognize and respond appropriately to medical and behavioral changes
✓ Provide compassionate end-of-life care
✓ Support families through the grieving process
✓ Maintain professional boundaries and ethical standards
✓ Comply with HIPAA and confidentiality requirements
✓ Work effectively in an interdisciplinary team environment
✓ Apply evidence-based practices in patient care

PROGRAM CURRICULUM
================================================================================

MODULE 1: FOUNDATIONS OF DIRECT SUPPORT
- Role and responsibilities of direct support professionals
- Ethical principles in healthcare
- Introduction to hospice and palliative care
- Professional boundaries and communication

MODULE 2: PATIENT CARE FUNDAMENTALS
- Basic nursing concepts and patient assessment
- Infection control and safety procedures
- Hygiene and personal care assistance
- Nutrition and hydration management
- Medication awareness

MODULE 3: EMOTIONAL & SPIRITUAL SUPPORT
- Understanding grief and loss
- Therapeutic communication techniques
- Spiritual care and cultural sensitivity
- Family dynamics and support
- Self-care and stress management

MODULE 4: END-OF-LIFE CARE
- Stages of dying and what to expect
- Pain and symptom management
- Comfort care measures
- Advance directives and end-of-life decisions
- Post-death care and family support

MODULE 5: WORKING IN HOSPICE
- Interdisciplinary team roles
- Documentation and record-keeping
- Legal and regulatory requirements
- Quality improvement and best practices
- Challenges and resilience

PROGRAM REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

Prerequisite: ☐ High School Diploma or GED
             ☐ Basic healthcare knowledge

Hours: 40 hours instruction + 10 hours supervised practice

Duration: 2-3 months (flexible schedule)

Delivery: ☐ In-person workshops
         ☐ Online modules
         ☐ Hybrid (combination)
         ☐ On-the-job training

